=== plain-80: width 80, height 24, profile notty, dark, glyphs ascii, plain
# play backup/runs ---------------------------------------------$
$
# Note$
# Play mode, mocks: the Backup screen proposed for slice 3,$
# drawn from what real code reads of a simulated host, each$
# change on the real plan/apply engine. Nothing on this machine$
# changes: every command and file is the fake's, and its record$
# is shown when play ends.$
$
# Info: backup/runs$
# web-01.example.net runs Debian 13. Three earlier changes were$
# backed up to /var/backups/hardn: an SSH port, a DNS change,$
# then a save with backups off; hardn.yml and resolv.conf have$
# changed since. Each change is planned, reviewed, confirmed y/N$
# and applied on the real engine; then the screen is read again.$
$
# Backup Settings ##############################################$
$
# Backup Configuration -----------------------------------------$
$
  [+] Backup State         Enabled$
  [+] Backup Path          /var/backups/hardn Root only$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Backup State         Turn backups off$
   2) Backup Path          Change backup path$
   3) Verify Directory     Check the path, writing nothing$
   4) Backup Runs          3 runs$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-4 or q]: 4$
$
# Backup Runs ##################################################$
$
  Select a run$
$
   1) 2026-10-19 14:30     1 file, taken anyway$
   2) 2026-10-18 09:15     2 files$
   3) 2026-10-17 08:30     1 file$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-3 or q]: 3$
$
# Backup Run ###################################################$
$
# Run 20261017T083000Z-9c0d1e2f --------------------------------$
$
   -  /etc/ssh/sshd_config.d/00-hardn.conf$
      Not there before$
$
  Select an option$
$
   1) Restore              Put these files back$
$
   0) Return$
$
  > Enter selection [0-1 or q]: 1$
$
